The '''''Liberator''''', serving temporarily as '''''Phoenix Home''''', was a [[CR90 corvette]] in the service of the [[Phoenix Cell]] in the [[Standard year|years]] prior to the [[Battle of Yavin]]. She served as the flagship of the Phoenix rebels following the destruction of the original command ship ''[[Phoenix Home]]'' during an [[Attack on Phoenix Squadron (4 BBY)|attack]] by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]].<ref name="Siege">''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Siege of Lothal]]''</ref> Unfortunately, she had a tendency to run into trouble due to this status, and twice only escaped capture thanks to the [[Spectres]]. She would later be succeeded as Phoenix Home by a stolen Imperial carrier, ''[[Phoenix Nest]]''. She became one of the first ships to join the newly-formed Alliance to Restore the Republic and ultimately one of three cruisers to survive the disastrous Battle of Atollon.

==History==
===The rebellion===
[[File:Explosion_of_the_Imperial_Interdictor.png|thumb|left|200px|The ''Liberator'' escaping from an Imperial interdictor]]
The ''Liberator'' was a [[CR90 corvette]] that was part of the [[Phoenix Cell]]. She and two other CR90s participated in the rescue of Kanan Jarrus over Mustafar, destroying multiple TIE fighters and saving the otherwise trapped Spectres. After an [[Attack on Phoenix Squadron (4 BBY)|attack]] on the Phoenix fleet by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], who destroyed the [[command ship]] ''[[Phoenix Home]]'', Phoenix [[Commander]] [[Jun Sato]] transferred his command to the ''Liberator''.<ref name="Sato Databank" /> To distinguish her from the other corvettes in the fleet, the ''Liberator'' was given a blue paint job that almost entirely covered her hull. At some point during the conflict, the ''Liberator'' was transporting Commander Sato and [[Ezra Bridger]] when it was suddenly pulled out of hyperspace by an [[Interdictor (Interdictor-class)|Imperial Interdictor]], an Imperial warship equipped with [[gravity well projector]]s. The ''Liberator'' had been investigating the disappearance of a rebel patrol in the [[Del Zennis system]].<ref name="Stealth Strike">{{Rebels|Stealth Strike}}</ref>

Following the capture of the ''Liberator'' and her crew, [[Phoenix Leader]] [[Hera Syndulla]] sent [[Kanan Jarrus]], [[Captain]] [[Rex]], and [[C1-10P|Chopper]] to rescue the ship's crew and Ezra. The rebels succeeded in rescuing Ezra along with Commander Sato and his crew. After picking up Kanan and Rex in an escape pod, the ''Liberator'' attempted to jump out of the system but was once again torn back out of it by the gravity wells. However, Chopper had previously sabotaged the Imperial Interdictor's gravity well projectors to affect all nearby ships and it also drew in the [[Arquitens-class command cruiser|''Arquitens''-class command cruisers]] protecting the Interdictor. The collision of the Interdictor and the light cruisers disrupted the gravity field seconds before the corvette impacted as well and the ''Liberator'' veered off as the Interdictor imploded, to her crew's jubilation. The ''Liberator'' and her passengers then escaped into [[hyperspace]] where they rejoined the Phoenix fleet.<ref name="Stealth Strike" />

The ''Liberator'' and the rest of the Phoenix rebels, devoid of a permanent base, hid within the [[spaceport]]s of [[Garel]], an [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] planet near [[Lothal]]. After the Empire discovered the rebel presence on Garel, the ''Liberator'' and the rest of the Phoenix fleet braved the Imperial blockade to escape into space, though one of her Taylander shuttle escorts was lost to enemy fire. While attempting to escape Garel, the ''Liberator'' was caught in the [[tractor beam]] of the [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|Imperial Star Destroyer]] ''[[Relentless]]''. However, Hera managed to free the ''Liberator'' by ramming the ''Ghost'' into the Star Destroyer's [[tractor beam projector]]; allowing Commander Sato and his crew along with Rex to escape into hyperspace.<ref name="Legacy">{{Rebels|Legacy (episode)}}</ref>

[[File:Heras_damaged_starfighter.png|thumb|right|200px|The ''Liberator'' intercepting Hera's damaged starfighter following a dogfight above Concord Dawn]]
The ''Liberator{{'s}}'' conference room later hosted a meeting between Commander Sato, Rex, and the crew of the ''Ghost'' to discuss their options for opening a new [[hyperspace]] route into the [[Lothal sector]]. During the meeting, the rebels decided to send a diplomatic mission to seek permission from the [[Journeyman Protector|Mandalorian Protectors]], a [[Mandalorian]] faction, to allow them safe passage through the [[Concord Dawn system]]. This mission was headed by Phoenix Leader Hera. However, Hera's mission was [[Dogfight over Concord Dawn|attacked]] above [[Concord Dawn]] by Protectors, whose leader [[Fenn Rau]] had sided with the Empire. Following the failed mission, Hera was treated by a [[2-1B surgical droid]] in the ''Liberator{{'s}}'' [[medical bay]].<ref name="The Protector of Concord Dawn">{{Rebels|The Protector of Concord Dawn}}</ref>

The ''Liberator{{'s}}'' conference room hosted a debriefing attended by the rebels with the exception of Hera. During that meeting, the rebels decided to send a sabotage mission headed by Kanan to destroy the Protectors' [[Fang-class Protectorate fighter|Fang fighters]], which were housed in a [[Protectors Camp|base]] on the [[third moon of Concord Dawn]]. This [[Mission to the third moon of Concord Dawn|mission]] succeeded in destroying the Protectors' starfighters there and capturing Rau, who agreed to allow the rebels safe passage through the Concord Dawn system in return for keeping his capture a secret from the Empire.<ref name="The Protector of Concord Dawn" />

Not long after the Concord Dawn incident, the Phoenix fleet stole a ''Quasar Fire''-class cruiser-carrier from Ryloth which became the new ''Phoenix Home'', though the Liberator continued to faithfully serve the fleet. It, along with the carrier and the trio of Hammerhead corvettes, participated in a short [[Attack on Phoenix Squadron (3 BBY)|battle]] with [[Admiral]] [[Kassius Konstantine]]'s fleet in space but successfully escaped to the isolated planet Atollon after Chopper provided coordinates.<ref name="TFD">{{Rebels|The Forgotten Droid}}</ref>

Not long after the establishment of [[Chopper Base]], the ''Liberator'' transported Ezra Bridger and Kanan Jarrus in a mission to rendezvous with another rebel transport, the [[Sphyrna-class Hammerhead corvette|''Sphyrna''-class Hammerhead corvette]] [[P3]]. Upon exiting hyperspace, however, they found that P3 had been attacked and heavily damaged. The ''Liberator'' came alongside the damaged Hammerhead and docked with her, allowing Ezra and Kanan to explore the ship and find out what happened. They learned from an injured rebel crewman that a "red blade" had attacked them and that the ''Ghost'' was in danger. Returning to the ''Liberator'', the two Jedi contacted the ''Ghost'' but discovered to their horror that the former [[Sith Lord]] [[Maul]] had already captured them, threatening to kill them unless he was given the Sith holocron Ezra had taken from [[Malachor]]. After a tense exchange, Ezra and Kanan agreed to his demands and the ''Liberator'' shuttled them back to Atollon to recover it.<ref name="The Holocrons of Fate">{{Rebels|The Holocrons of Fate}}</ref>

[[File:Iron_Squadron_26.jpg|thumb|left|200px|The ''Liberator'' helped Iron Squadron to escape from Mykapo]]
The ''Liberator'' later took part in a skirmish above the planet [[Mykapo]]. After the Ghost crew returned to the system to help rescue [[Mart Mattin]] and his [[Iron Squadron]], Commander Sato arrived late to the battle with the ''Liberator'' and a pair of A-wings. The CR-90 destroyed the opposing forces with ease, destroying a Gozanti cruiser and inflicting damage to Konstantine's light cruiser. After the skirmish, the ''Liberator'' came face to face with Grand Admiral Thrawn but quickly made her escape into hyperspace.<ref name="Iron Squadron">{{Rebels|Iron Squadron (episode)}}</ref>

===Service to the Alliance===
The ''Liberator'' was part of the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|rebel fleet]] that joined [[Mon Mothma]] at [[Dantooine]] after her broadcast in which she vowed not to rest until they defeated the [[Galactic Empire|Empire]] and restored the Republic.<ref name="Secret Cargo" />

[[File:AftermathAtollon.jpg|thumb|right|200px|The ''Liberator'' was one of the remaining ships after the Battle of Atollon.]]
The ''Liberator'' was part of the fleet that was stationed at [[Atollon]] during the [[Battle of Atollon]], engaging Thrawn's Seventh Fleet alongside ships from the Massassi Group. After suffering severe casualties, the rebels managed to flee in defeat. The ''Liberator'' was the sole surviving CR90 corvette from the engagement and, along with the Hammerhead corvettes P1 and P3, the only rebel cruisers to escape. After three successive hyperspace jumps to shake off pursuit, the ''Liberator'' and the remaining rebels journeyed to [[Yavin 4]].<ref name="Zero Hour" />

